e 1-line from above and below. The lone 4-pixel, whose colour has no line, simply vanishes.\n- Pair 2 (vertical lines: 3 at x=3, 4 at x=12): the 4-pixels at (3,1) and (7,9) both move to column 11 (left side of the 4-line) in their own rows; the 3-pixels at (3,6) and (11,16) move to column 4 (right side of the 3-line). The 2-pixel vanishes.\n- Pair 3 (one horizontal 8-line at row 5): the 8-pixels slide to rows 4 or 6 depending on which side they started; both 1-pixels vanish.\n\nSo the rule is: **every stray pixel slides straight toward the line of its own colour until it touches it, staying on the side it started on; pixels with no matching line are erased.** Nothing else changes – the lines themselves stay put.\n\n**Applying it to the test input.** It has three vertical lines: 2 at x=4, 3 at x=11, 4 at x=20. The 2-pixels (2,16) and (10,1) go to (2,5) and (10,3); the 3-pixels (9,13), (15,8), (17,22) go to (9,12), (15,10), (17,12); the 4-pixels (7,6), (4,24)… wait, (4,24) is colour 8 – the 4-pixels are (7,6) and (15,24), which go to (7,19) and (15,21). All four 8-pixels have no 8-line, so they are erased.\n\n**Construction stages emitted.** First I erase the pixels that have no matching line, then I move each remaining pixel to its spot next to its line, emitting after each move.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    # full-length single-colour lines\n    hlines = {}  # colour -> row\n    vlines = {}  # colour -> col\n    for y in range(H):\n        if len(set(g[y, :])) == 1 and g[y, 0] != bg:\n            hlines[int(g[y, 0])] = y\n    for x in range(W):\n        if len(set(g[:, x])) == 1 and g[0, x] != bg:\n            vlines[int(g[0, x])] = x\n\n    def on_line(y, x):\n        return y in hlines.values() or x in vlines.values()\n\n    # stray pixels (not part of a line)\n    strays = [(y, x, int(g[y, x])) for y in range(H) for x in range(W)\n              if g[y, x] != bg and not on_line(y, x)]\n\n    # stage 1: erase pixels whose colour has no line\n    removed = False\n    for y, x, c in strays:\n        if c not in hlines and c not in vlines:\n            out[y, x] = bg\n            removed = True\n    if removed:\n        emit(out.copy(), \"erase stray pixels whose colour has no matching line\")\n\n    # stage 2: slide each remaining pixel to touch its line, on its own side\n    for y, x, c in strays:\n        if c in hlines:\n            r = hlines[c]\n            ny, nx = (r - 1 if y < r else r + 1), x\n        elif c in vlines:\n            cc = vlines[c]\n            ny, nx = y, (cc - 1 if x < cc else cc + 1)\n        else:\n            continue\n        out[y, x] = bg\n        out[ny, nx] = c\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"move colour-{c} pixel from ({y},{x}) to ({ny},{nx}), touching its line\")\n\n    emit(out.copy(), \"final\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 3 (one horizontal 8-line at row 5): the 8-pixels slide to rows 4 or 6 depending on which side they started; both 1-pixels vanish."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"So the rule is: **every stray pixel slides straight toward the line of its own colour until it touches it, staying on the side it started on; pixels with no matching line are erased.** Nothing else changes – the lines themselves stay put."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Construction stages emitted.** First I erase the pixels that have no matching line, then I move each remaining pixel to its spot next to its line, emitting after each move."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"68451af73b21767cc64e8ed73fbe89fa52e1f86f864134de85a63b3110b6ced1","task_sha256":"9804ccdabaa67922fdd44143e90bf351d2d8bd8c612b6e3cb47f498edf3492ea","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
